106
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Well, there is a concern in some departments that there is low staff morale.

107
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:18,000
This is indicated by the recent low sales figures and also increased sickness absence in some of the departments.

108
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
I'm sorry, I don't seem to have the report.

109
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Thank you.

110
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Right, well, there seems to be a significance problem with staff morale in the sales team and also sickness absence and also company-wide, particularly on Mondays and Fridays.

111
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,000
There is definitely low morale in the company in certain departments.

112
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
New changes have been introduced, like the IT system.

113
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:46,000
People just want to know why certain people have left, why there's been restructuring and whether their jobs are safe.

114
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Yeah, isn't this just gossip? Sounds like excuses and laziness to me.

115
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Anyway, it clearly is the case that sales figures are at their lowest since February last year and it's mainly to do with the amount of absences from the sales team.

116
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:07,000
The recent launch of Comet Software has caused problems too because it seems that people haven't had enough training and are therefore making a number of mistakes.

117
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
I've done my best. It's a big department.

118
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:21,000
I would like to say that the basic instruction handout was given out and everyone was shown step-by-step easy steps about how this should be done and everyone was provided with a...

119
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Well, should have been provided...

120
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Well, no, actually they were provided with a password that would allow them to log into the new system.

121
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:37,000
OK, so what has this got to do with staff morale? It's with people struggling with new software, you know, they're making mistakes, it slows them down, it demotivates them.

122
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Anyway, if you could all look at the second report, Lucy and I produced an anonymous questionnaire to get feedback from staff about issues.

123
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:52,000
If you have a look, you'll see very clearly the feedback statistics.

124
00:07:52,000 --> 00:08:01,000
And, Lucy, I don't mean to pick on you, but you were given a password and, like everyone else, you seem to have mislaid it or lost it and then you emailed me...

125
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:08,000
What is this losing or forgetting passwords got to do with low morale? And also, everyone puts down poor management when you talk about morale.

126
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
It's just a waste of time, these questionnaires.

127
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Look, there are issues that have been raised, things like lack of training, lack of effective appraisals...

128
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
I do appraisals.

129
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Well, when was the last time you conducted a staff appraisal? Anyway, the point is that we need to be working a little harder to get people on side and we also found out from the questionnaire that some of the issues are to do with the recent restructuring, the job losses, poor management in some departments and also, as I've mentioned, the lack of training on the new software.

130
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Well, thank you for that, Sue.

131
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
You do seem to have taken on a lot recently.

132
00:08:47,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Look, as there are a few reasons, what would you say was the predominant reason so that we can begin to tackle one at a time, maybe start work on the major one first? Well, I think it might be a good idea if you and I had a separate meeting about that.

133
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Why don't we move on to the second issue now? Well, OK, we can hold on that, but maybe we could have one after this meeting.

134
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
OK.

135
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
But, you know, Sue, these issues really need to be dealt with now.

136
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
OK, I take your point, but I do wish Clive was here.

137
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
OK, maybe we could discuss the new appraisal system now.

138
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
We could have an awards night.

139
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
